    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s strongest plays today are headlined by **Bryson Stott** (72.46) and **Lawrence Butler** (68.54), both of whom benefit significantly from positive platoon dynamics and favorable matchups against right-handed pitching. **Bryson Stott** is our highest-rated starter, bolstered by a 16% SP skill advantage against Miles Mikolas and a robust 13% platoon boost. Similarly, **Lawrence Butler** leverages an identical 13% platoon edge against Tyler Mahle, compounded by a wind-out scenario at his venue. **Daulton Varsho** (65.71) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (63.13) round out our top-tier starters; **Daulton Varsho** utilizes a strong 10% platoon advantage against Mike Burrows, while **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from an 8% boost for holding down the #2 spot in the order against a vulnerable Matthew Liberatore.\n\nWe have a clear prioritization of high-contact and speed-oriented profiles, evidenced by the inclusion of **Tyler Freeman** (61.08), who overcomes a neutral platoon matchup through a massive 14% park factor adjustment. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Jung Hoo Lee** (46.32), who narrowly missed the cut for the final outfield slot. While **Jung Hoo Lee** remains a high-floor asset, the optimizer favored the specific situational volatility of **Gavin Sheets** and the park-factor upside afforded to **Tyler Freeman**. We continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while keeping a close eye on **Yainer Diaz** and **Cal Raleigh**; both catchers are currently subject to \"Lineup Pending\" designations, meaning their sub-60 scores could fluctuate based on official confirmation of their placement in the batting order.",
